ty_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":27,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've patched the network to remove an end-of-episode deadlock. `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are written.\n\n**What I changed and why:** In one of the six recorded start-network episodes, the network kept EW_through green after demand stopped, with no E/W traffic. Three vehicles on other approaches waited about 1,800 s, until the cap. Synthetic traces show this happens often: with one to three cars left on almost any other lane, it holds EW_through forever. I added a veto for all four phases: a phase with no vehicle on its stop-line or upstream lanes loses 40 from its logit. When the whole junction is empty, the original choice stands.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 368 of 7428. Four layer-1 units became emptiness detectors and four layer-2 units became gates, with their outgoing weights and the biases adjusted to match.\n\n**Checks:**\n- On recorded traffic, about 0.6% of honoured decisions change, all near-ties (top-2 logit gap ≤ 0.36).\n- 0 of 49,140 sparse end-of-episode traces deadlock, against 87 for the original.\n- In 200,000 random sparse states it never picks an empty phase while another phase has vehicles.\n- The recorded deadlock state is now served.\n\n**Predictions (veh-h):** low 34.45, nominal 44.65, high 54.15. That is about 0.25 below the start network's dev scores. If no test episode deadlocks, the gain is about zero, and seed noise of ±0.5 veh-h could hide it.","ttft_ms":1085,"type":"result","duration_ms":878769,"uuid":"8bd51e63-a995-4f88-98a6-5ddb79751339","ttft_stream_ms":887,"time_to_request_ms":43,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact"